# Note: this is for aviation usage, so this is jet fuel. Steam turbine vehicles (i.e. turbine steamships) should be coded in the vehicle .dat files as "steam".
# 2024-2026 applied as year-on-year changes in the IATA/Platts jet fuel price:
# 2024 about -10% (100.4 USD/bbl against 111 in 2023), 2025 -9.2% (91.1),
# 2026 +67% (IATA forecast 152 USD/bbl after the Strait of Hormuz disruption).
# Units: litres
fuel[turbine]=1750,100,1950,192,1951,211,1952,271,1953,284,1954,284,1955,289,1956,340,1957,324,1958,299,1959,296,1960,311,1961,311,1962,303,1963,321,1964,329,1965,345,1966,345,1967,393,1968,414,1969,425,1970,204,1971,252,1972,252,1973,276,1974,408,1975,696,1976,816,1977,1020,1978,1080,1979,1080,1980,1992,1981,2438,1982,2617,1983,2780,1984,2959,1985,2661,1986,2528,1987,2542,1988,2763,1989,3174,1990,3391,1991,3311,1992,3680,1993,3859,1994,4065,1995,4153,1996,4546,1997,4802,1998,5219,1999,5784,2000,5472,2001,5338,2002,5477,2003,2804,2004,2124,2005,3016,2006,4588,2007,3781,2008,5905,2009,3696,2010,5395,2011,7477,2012,8624,2013,8836,2014,7604,2015,4885,2016,2889,2017,5268,2018,5607,2019,6245,2020,4928,2021,4928,2022,8411,2023,7764,2024,7019,2025,6373,2026,10643,2050,17796

# Horses have no specific fuel cost, per se - fodder cost should be part of fixed maintenance. 
fuel[bio]=1750,0,2050,0

fuel[sail]=1750,0,2050,0

# Units: kw/h
# 1890 datum guessed for now as the research based figures were missing this datum.
# 2017-2026 rebased on 2026-11-15. The coal row of the balancing workbook gives
# 0.53 GBP/ton in 1900 = 10 units, i.e. a .dat unit is 1/192 of a penny, so the
# value is the nominal price in pence per kWh x 192. That rule reproduces the
# coal series (1950: 47) and the road fuels within a few per cent, and this
# series matches it within 5% up to 2013; the old 2017-2026 block ran 28-59%
# high. 2026 is estimated from the Q1-Q2 quarters (about 24.0p per kWh).
